  "comparison_limits": [
    "The 3090J and 3090V GPUs are both RTX 3090 Ti, but their production model files differ despite identical filenames.",
    "J and V require a common model and matched context, cache, MTP and batching controls for throughput comparison.",
    "J driver 570.211.01 differs from V driver 615.71.09; CPU, RAM and PCIe topology also differ. Cross-host differences cannot isolate the unlock.",
    "J GPU is attached through an upstream port with maximum width x4; V GPU reports x16. The x4 upstream limit is independent of idle link generation. Generation must also be recorded under load.",
    "Verified UTC unlock success anchors are V 2026-10-25T13:11:45.282904+00:00 and 4090 2026-10-26T02:18:08.390111+00:00. Historical runs after their worker-specific anchor were already unlocked and cannot be pre-unlock baselines; earlier Oct 25/26 measurements must be classified individually.",
    "Boot journal success verifies that the module reported unlocking that PCI device. Current selector readback was not performed.",
    "A user change to dotenv does not prove a running llama-server uses ubatch 1024; the registry cannot establish its effective process argv.",
    "No same-card, same-driver locked-versus-unlocked causal A/B was performed.",
    "RAM and swap figures are instantaneous host snapshots; free swap is not a latency or capacity guarantee."
  ],
